# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-14, R-3, RC-1, G1 Q-4). L §5.14.3: "Labels are walk state: the walk at cut K labels every
# movement, planned or observed, by the arrival rule read at K ... So a later ruling about whose past money was applies
# under every cut that sees it, ... and as known D shows the labels before it"; "The one exception: parts ... a past
# decision that no observation fulfils, and whose amount or when reads parts (bal(x) of p ...), follows a later version
# that changes whose past money was ... under every cut that sees that version ... Its law and its other facts stay
# those known on its day." The ruling (known 2026-06-01) makes a1's 100.00 tomek's: under the model's cut the sweep of
# tomek's parts on 2026-04-01 takes 100.00 times frac as known on its day (1, not the ruling's 0.5); as known
# 2026-05-01, ania's, and the sweep takes 0.00 (figures carried: a1's 100.00).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order if k.owner == ania then 0 else 1
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input a1_day: date
input a1_amt: money PLN
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule base = if p == ania then 1 else 0
input sweep_day: date
input frac: num
move sweep: transfers
  on sweep_day
  reads konto
  leg cash from konto to shop amount round((bal(konto) of tomek) * frac, minor(PLN), half-even)
move a1: transfers
  on a1_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount a1_amt
ask q1: bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of ania, bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of tomek, flows(sweep, 2026-04), bal(konto, 2026-04-30)
ask q2: bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of ania, bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of tomek, flows(sweep, 2026-04), bal(konto, 2026-04-30) as known 2026-05-01

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  a1_day = 2026-02-01
  a1_amt = 100.00 PLN
  sweep_day = 2026-04-01
  frac = 1

version ruling
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-06-01
  replace rule arrive.base = if p == tomek then 1 else 0
  replace frac = 0.5
=== expect
q1: (0.00 PLN, 100.00 PLN, 100.00 PLN, 0.00 PLN)
  unfulfilled: a1
  unfulfilled: sweep
  cut 2026-10-01
q2: (100.00 PLN, 0.00 PLN, 0.00 PLN, 100.00 PLN)
  unfulfilled: a1
  unfulfilled: sweep
  cut 2026-05-01
